/-
# Locally finitely stable realizations (Kourovka Notebook Problem 2.58)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.58 (B. I. Plotkin): let `G` be a vector
space and `Γ` a group of automorphisms of `G`. `Γ` is called locally finitely stable if, for any
finitely generated subgroup `Δ` of `Γ`, `G` has a finite series stable relative to `Δ`. If the
characteristic of the field is zero and `Γ` is locally finitely stable, then `Γ` is locally
nilpotent and torsion-free. Is it true that every locally nilpotent torsion-free group can be
realized in this way?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.LocallyNilpotentShared
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.StableSeriesShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFinitelyStableRealizationKourovka2Problem58Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.58 (B. I.
Plotkin). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700129 (`KOU-2.58`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A set of linear automorphisms is stable when some finite chain of subspaces `0 = W₀ ≤ W₁ ≤ ⋯ ≤ W_m =
V` satisfies `g w - w ∈ W_i` for every element `g` of the set and every `w ∈ W_{i+1}` (a chain of
additive subgroups with this property spans such a chain of subspaces, so nothing depends on using
subspaces). Groups of automorphisms of `V` are subgroups of the group `V ≃ₗ[K] V` of linear
automorphisms. `HasStableSeries` is shared with the other stable-series entries in
`WantedExt.GroupTheory.StableSeriesShared`. Locally nilpotent is `IsLocallyNilpotent ⊤` (shared in
`WantedExt.GroupTheory.LocallyNilpotentShared`). Realized means isomorphic to such a group: a
faithful representation `ρ : G →* (V ≃ₗ[K] V)` over some field `K` of characteristic `0` in which
the image of every finitely generated subgroup of `G` (generated by a finite set `s`) has a finite
stable series.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.StableSeriesShared MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyNilpotentShared

/-- Kourovka 2.58 (B. I. Plotkin): every locally nilpotent torsion-free group is isomorphic to a
locally finitely stable group of automorphisms of a vector space over a field of characteristic
`0`: there is a faithful linear representation `ρ` in which the image of every finitely
generated subgroup has a finite stable series. -/
def locallyNilpotentTorsionFreeIsLocallyFinitelyStable : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], IsLocallyNilpotent (⊤ : Subgroup G) →
    (∀ g : G, g ≠ 1 → ¬ IsOfFinOrder g) →
    ∃ (K : Type) (_ : Field K) (_ : CharZero K) (V : Type) (_ : AddCommGroup V) (_ : Module K V)
      (ρ : G →* (V ≃ₗ[K] V)), Function.Injective ρ ∧
        ∀ s : Finset G, HasStableSeries (ρ '' (Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) : Set G))

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 2.58 "No", citing Simonyan (1971): some locally
nilpotent torsion-free group is not isomorphic to a locally finitely stable group of automorphisms
of a vector space over a field of characteristic zero. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov
(eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49
(2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.58 (B. I. Plotkin); resolution: L. A. Simonyan,
Siberian Math. J. 12 (1971), 602-606, Kourovka Archive, Problem 2.58: No (Simonyan),
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted locallyNilpotentTorsionFreeIsLocallyFinitelyStable_refuted :
    ¬ locallyNilpotentTorsionFreeIsLocallyFinitelyStable

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFinitelyStableRealizationKourovka2Problem58Wanted
